# Normalized visual mapping QA

Date: 2026-08-30
Project: `D:\Laragon\www\laravel-13-phoenix`
Scope: Recursive nested-DOM projection, composite block grouping, widget signatures, and v2.4 target payload integration.

## Implemented behavior

- Raw measured DOM remains available with source IDs, parent relationships, attributes, HTML, computed styles, rectangles, and viewport data.
- A separate normalized projection exposes `mappingRoots`, `mappingNodes`, `childMappingIds`, `memberSourceIds`, `mappingRole`, and `mappingKind`.
- Structural Grid/Flex wrappers remain layout nodes even when they contain media or icons.
- Layout-neutral wrappers are promoted without dropping their content.
- Semantic text elements with inline descendants remain one content mapping unit; `span`, `br`, and decorative `i` become members.
- `div > dt(icon/label) + dd(value)` is represented as an `icon_box` composite shape.
- `figure > img + overlay` is represented as an `image_box` composite shape with members retained for traceability.
- Thin textless visual rules are suggested as `divider`.
- High-confidence candidate widget types prefill the UI select; user selection remains editable and is the only value consumed by target compilation.
- Normalized/import-only metadata is stripped at the final Canvas payload boundary.

